{"id":"2aac531c-8f5f-4476-8d82-cf9768152c5a","object":"chat.completion","created":1785008290,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    if not isinstance(case, dict):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"case must be a dict\\\")\\n    if \\\"text\\\" not in case or not isinstance(case[\\\"text\\\"], str):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"missing or invalid 'text'\\\")\\n    if \\\"passes\\\" not in case or not isinstance(case[\\\"passes\\\"], list):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"missing or invalid 'passes'\\\")\\n    for p in case[\\\"passes\\\"]:\\n        if not isinstance(p, dict) or \\\"old\\\" not in p or \\\"new\\\" not in p or \\\"name\\\" not in p:\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"invalid pass entry\\\")\\n    if \\\"max_rounds\\\" not in case or not isinstance(case[\\\"max_rounds\\\"], int):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"missing or invalid 'max_rounds'\\\")\\n    artifact = case[\\\"text\\\"]\\n    applications = []\\n    max_rounds = case[\\\"max_rounds\\\"]\\n    passes = case[\\\"passes\\\"]\\n    for _ in range(max_rounds):\\n        changed = False\\n        for p in passes:\\n            old = p[\\\"old\\\"]\\n            new = p[\\\"new\\\"]\\n            pos = artifact.find(old)\\n            if pos != -1:\\n                artifact = artifact[:pos] + new + artifact[pos+len(old):]\\n                applications.append(p[\\\"name\\\"])\\n                changed = True\\n        if not changed:\\n            break\\n    fixed_point = not changed\\n    return {\\n        \\\"text\\\": artifact,\\n        \\\"applications\\\": applications,\\n        \\\"fixed_point\\\": fixed_point\\n    }\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to write a Python function `solve(case)` that takes a payload object (as per the fixture). The payload has fields: text (string), passes (list of objects each with name, old, new), max_rounds (int). Possibly other fields like _case_nonce but we only use needed fields.\n\nTask: Implement a fixed-point schedule. Description: \"Apply passes in their registered order. Each pass performs at most its first eligible rewrite per sweep. Record only passes that change the artifact. Repeat full sweeps until none changes or the round budget is consumed. Return the artifact, application trace, and fixed-point flag.\"\n\nOutput schema: object with \"applications\" (list of strings, pass names that changed artifact), \"fixed_point\" (bool), \"text\" (string, final artifact). \"text\" is the resulting string after applying transformations.\n\nInterpretation: There's a concept of \"artifact\" which is the text string being transformed. Each pass replaces all occurrences of \"old\" with \"new\" in the artifact? But description says \"first eligible rewrite per sweep\". Wait: \"Each pass performs at most its first eligible rewrite per sweep\". That suggests per sweep (i.e., per round of passes), each pass only applies its rewrite once (the first occurrence). But there is also \"Each pass performs at most its first eligible rewrite per sweep.\" That is ambiguous: does it mean that in each sweep, the pass only applies to the first occurrence of old in the current text? That would be a single replacement. But there is also \"Record only passes that change the artifact.\" So if a pass makes no change (no occurrence of old), it's not recorded. And we repeat full sweeps until no pass changes anything in a full sweep or max_rounds reached.\n\nThe fixture shows example passes: halve-a replaces \"aa\" with \"a\", drop-b replaces \"bb\" with \"b\", drop-c replaces \" cc\" with \"\". Input text \"aaaa bb cc\". Let's simulate: Sweep1: pass halve-a: find first occurrence of \"aa\" in \"aaaa bb cc\"? The string: first two chars \"aa\", replace with \"a\" => becomes \"aa bb cc\". Then pass drop-b: find first \"bb\" -> replace with \"b\" => \"aa b cc\". Then pass drop-c: find first \" cc\" -> replace with \"\" => \"aa b\". Sweep2: pass halve-a: find first \"aa\" in \"aa b\" -> replace with \"a\" => \"a b\". pass drop-b: find first \"bb\"? none -> no change. pass drop-c: find first \" cc\"? none -> no change. Sweep3: pass halve-a: find first \"aa\"? none -> no change. All passes no change, stop. So final text \"a b\". applications: [\"halve-a\", \"drop-b\", \"drop-c\", \"halve-a\"] (but note drop-c changed in sweep1, drop-b changed in sweep1, halve-a changed in sweep1 and sweep2). Actually drop-b changed in sweep1? Yes \"bb\" -> \"b\". So applications: list of names that changed artifact in order of occurrence across sweeps. That yields [\"halve-a\", \"drop-b\", \"drop-c\", \"halve-a\"]. The fixed_point is true because we reached a point where no further changes after round budget (max_rounds=8, but stopped earlier). If we hit max_rounds, fixed_point false.\n\nBut note: \"Each pass performs at most its first eligible rewrite per sweep.\" That suggests each pass only does one replacement per sweep, which matches replacement of first occurrence. So we must implement that.\n\nNow need to write code. Use Python standard library only.\n\nImplementation steps:\n- Validate input: case must have \"text\" (string), \"passes\" (list, each with \"old\" and \"new\" strings), \"max_rounds\" (int). If not, raise ValueError.\n- Initialize `artifact = case[\"text\"]`\n- Initialize `applications = []`\n- For round in range(case[\"max_rounds\"]):\n    - changed_this_sweep = False\n    - For each pass in case[\"passes\"]:\n        - old = pass[\"old\"]\n        new = pass[\"new\"]\n        - Find first occurrence of old in artifact. Use `artifact.find(old)`.\n        - If found:\n            - Replace only that occurrence: `artifact = artifact[:pos] + new + artifact[pos+len(old):]`\n            - Append pass[\"name\"] to applications.\n            - changed_this_sweep = True\n    - If not changed_this_sweep: break\n- fixed_point = (changed_this_sweep == False) or (round == max_rounds-1 and not changed? Actually fixed_point true if we broke because no changes in a full sweep. If we exhausted max_rounds without reaching fixed point, fixed_point false. So after loop, if we broke early due to no changes, fixed_point = True, else False.\nHowever note that if the loop completes all max_rounds without reaching fixed point, fixed_point False.\n- Return dict with \"text\": artifact, \"applications\": applications, \"fixed_point\": fixed_point.\n\nEdge cases: pass may have name missing? Not required per schema? But we assume well-formed. Also pass order should be preserved.\n\nNow produce output as JSON with \"implementation\" key containing the Python source as a JSON string.\n\nWe must ensure the solve function does not mutate case, and returns JSON-serializable object. Use standard Python dict.\n\nWrite the code in a string, escape newlines, backslashes, quotes.\n\nI'll write the implementation as a function.\n\nOne more thing: The description mentions \"registered restart, cache, and interestingness rules\" but those are not present in payload. The fixture payload only has text, passes, max_rounds. So we ignore those extra concepts; they are not part of the public inputs.\n\nAlso \"Validate every required field before computing a result.\" So check if keys exist and types are correct.\n\nWrite solve function:\n\ndef solve(case):\n    # Validation\n    if not isinstance(case, dict):\n        raise ValueError(\"case must be a dict\")\n    if \"text\" not in case or not isinstance(case[\"text\"], str):\n        raise ValueError(\"missing or invalid 'text'\")\n    if \"passes\" not in case or not isinstance(case[\"passes\"], list):\n        raise ValueError(\"missing or invalid 'passes'\")\n    for p in case[\"passes\"]:\n        if not isinstance(p, dict) or \"old\" not in p or \"new\" not in p or \"name\" not in p:\n            raise ValueError(\"invalid pass entry\")\n    if \"max_rounds\" not in case or not isinstance(case[\"max_rounds\"], int):\n        raise ValueError(\"missing or invalid 'max_rounds'\")\n    \n    artifact = case[\"text\"]\n    applications = []\n    max_rounds = case[\"max_rounds\"]\n    passes = case[\"passes\"]\n \n    for _ in range(max_rounds):\n        changed = False\n        for p in passes:\n            old = p[\"old\"]\n            new = p[\"new\"]\n            pos = artifact.find(old)\n            if pos != -1:\n                artifact = artifact[:pos] + new + artifact[pos+len(old):]\n                applications.append(p[\"name\"])\n                changed = True\n        if not changed:\n            break\n\n    fixed_point = not changed  # if we broke due to no changes, changed is False => fixed_point True\n    # but if we exhausted rounds and last round had changes, then fixed_point False.\n    # However changed variable is only set in loop; after loop if break due to no changes, changed=False => fixed_point True.\n    # If loop completed all max_rounds, after last iteration changed may be True or False. If last iteration changed something, then we didn't break; after loop changed is the value from last iteration. So fixed_point = (last iteration had no changes). That is exactly (not changed). So fine.\n    \n    return {\n        \"text\": artifact,\n        \"applications\": applications,\n        \"fixed_point\": fixed_point\n    }\n\nThat's it.\n\nNow produce JSON envelope.\n\nI'll format the code string, escape properly.\n\nFinal output must be a JSON object with key \"implementation\". No markdown.\n\nLet's construct: {\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\\\n    ...\"}\n\nI'll write it carefully."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1310,"completion_tokens":2201,"total_tokens":3511,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1280},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1799},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1280,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":30},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}